{"id": "EUVD-2026-93213", "enisaUuid": "c418793a-7b1a-3e67-8f6b-d4bc723c543d", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: bridge: vlan: fix bugs caused by switchdev deletion errors\n\nAllowing switchdev to prevent vlan deletion and error out in __vlan_del\ncould cause multiple different issues - inconsistent state, memory leaks\nwhen flushing, NULL pointer dereference on bridge error when flushing.\nIt doesn't make sense to allow it to stop __vlan_del, so log the error\nand continue with software vlan deletion. This is also consistent with\n8021q behaviour.", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T08:45:46", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:16:56", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ed3ea86db736a30bebf49b947c42730e8451bcd2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2842ce397dd09882530b42f7fdb0c855767eb24e"], "aliases": ["GHSA-9v49-jvp7-mg86", "CVE-2026-98285"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "78271240-9d75-3d35-8611-6b2f945a01b3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.8"}, {"id": "8d9ff26b-204e-394e-9bdc-bf71a38e1daf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bf361ad38165939049a2649b1a0078f3268d4bd1 <2842ce397dd09882530b42f7fdb0c855767eb24e"}, {"id": "a4b5dc3d-284f-3c29-b0f7-4c83044ca83a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.3"}, {"id": "ac31fa41-9cbf-3bb2-a885-68fd9eebc5d2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "d9062e30-22cf-39af-89cb-a89d61c06087", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "f9bd6528-3ffe-3020-97ce-f787d86d287c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bf361ad38165939049a2649b1a0078f3268d4bd1 <ed3ea86db736a30bebf49b947c42730e8451bcd2"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "f093ec05-